  🛑  Requirement: Poll for the fork count instead of using a fixed sleep

  If GitHub takes more than five seconds to update the upstream's fork count, this test fails before exercising either
  deletion path. Replace the sleep and one-shot lookup with bounded polling until the count is 1, failing on timeout
  before attempting deletion. This follows the condition-based wait requirement in
  .github/skills/writing-acceptance-tests/SKILL.md:94-96 and the existing wait-for-repository-ready helper pattern.
